+# Kai Rivera's student-success survey learning plan
+
+## Learner snapshot
+
+Kai Rivera is a community-college advisor preparing to analyze a student-success survey and present evidence-based recommendations at a department meeting. Kai is comfortable with spreadsheets but new to statistics, so the sequence starts with familiar data-handling work and adds interpretation in small, applied steps.
+
+## Planning constraints
+
+- Duration: eight weeks, beginning the week of 2026-09-14.
+- Cadence: three 45-minute sessions each week—Tuesday at 7:00 PM, Wednesday at 7:00 PM, and Saturday at 10:00 AM.
+- Resources: one catalog item per week, used in the listed order.
+- Access: materials and outputs stay text-first and screen-reader-friendly. Charts use direct labels, patterns, and written descriptions, so meaning never depends on color alone.
+- Outcome: clean the survey spreadsheet, describe patterns without overclaiming, create an accessible chart, and finish a one-page recommendation memo with five-minute briefing notes for the department meeting.
+
+## Eight-week schedule
+
+| Week | Tuesday session | Wednesday session | Saturday session | Core resource | Applied deliverable |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Week 1 | 2026-09-15, 7:00 PM (45 min): Identify the department's decision question and mark ambiguous survey items. | 2026-09-16, 7:00 PM (45 min): Classify question types and note what each response can support. | 2026-09-19, 10:00 AM (45 min): Draft a text-first measurement map linking questions to cautious claims. | EDU-01 — Survey Questions and Measurement | A measurement map with the decision question, usable fields, limitations, and questions for the survey owner. |
+| Week 2 | 2026-09-22, 7:00 PM (45 min): Make a working copy and inventory columns, formats, blanks, and duplicates. | 2026-09-23, 7:00 PM (45 min): Apply documented cleaning rules while preserving the raw values. | 2026-09-26, 10:00 AM (45 min): Recheck counts and record every transformation in plain language. | EDU-02 — Spreadsheet Cleaning Patterns | A cleaned survey spreadsheet plus a concise, reproducible cleaning log and data dictionary. |
+| Week 3 | 2026-09-29, 7:00 PM (45 min): Calculate counts, percentages, and simple distributions for priority questions. | 2026-09-30, 7:00 PM (45 min): Compare typical values and spread using beginner-friendly summaries. | 2026-10-03, 10:00 AM (45 min): Write findings that separate observations from interpretations. | EDU-03 — Describing Data | A descriptive summary of three important patterns with the supporting counts and denominators. |
+| Week 4 | 2026-10-06, 7:00 PM (45 min): Identify who answered, who may be missing, and where nonresponse matters. | 2026-10-07, 7:00 PM (45 min): Practice explaining sampling and uncertainty without technical shorthand. | 2026-10-10, 10:00 AM (45 min): Revise earlier findings to state limitations without overclaiming. | EDU-04 — Sampling and Uncertainty | An uncertainty note pairing each key finding with a limitation and a defensible interpretation. |
+| Week 5 | 2026-10-13, 7:00 PM (45 min): Choose two useful group comparisons tied to the department question. | 2026-10-14, 7:00 PM (45 min): Check denominators and avoid treating small differences as decisive. | 2026-10-17, 10:00 AM (45 min): Draft neutral comparison language and note alternative explanations. | EDU-05 — Honest Comparisons | A comparison table with group counts, percentages, caveats, and two claims that avoid causal overreach. |
+| Week 6 | 2026-10-20, 7:00 PM (45 min): Select one finding whose structure is clearer visually than in prose. | 2026-10-21, 7:00 PM (45 min): Build the chart with direct labels, readable contrast, and no color-only distinctions. | 2026-10-24, 10:00 AM (45 min): Add alt text and a plain-language interpretation, then check reading order. | EDU-06 — Accessible Charts | An accessible chart with direct labels, alt text, source note, and a written takeaway. |
+| Week 7 | 2026-10-27, 7:00 PM (45 min): Rank possible recommendations by evidence strength and advisor relevance. | 2026-10-28, 7:00 PM (45 min): Link each recommendation to a finding, limitation, and practical next step. | 2026-10-31, 10:00 AM (45 min): Outline the memo and test whether every claim is supported. | EDU-07 — From Evidence to Recommendations | A recommendation outline connecting evidence, caveats, actions, and measures for follow-up. |
+| Week 8 | 2026-11-03, 7:00 PM (45 min): Draft the one-page recommendation memo around the decision and strongest evidence. | 2026-11-04, 7:00 PM (45 min): Write five-minute briefing notes with a clear opening, chart explanation, and ask. | 2026-11-07, 10:00 AM (45 min): Edit both products for accuracy, accessibility, timing, and meeting readiness. | EDU-08 — Briefing Memo Studio | A final one-page recommendation memo, accessible chart, and five-minute briefing notes for the department meeting. |
+
+## Completion checklist
+
+- [ ] Preserve the untouched raw survey and finish the cleaning log and data dictionary.
+- [ ] Verify every reported count, percentage, denominator, and comparison against the cleaned spreadsheet.
+- [ ] Pair each finding and recommendation with an appropriate uncertainty or limitation.
+- [ ] Check the chart's direct labels, contrast, reading order, alt text, and plain-language description.
+- [ ] Keep the recommendation memo to one page and connect every proposed action to evidence.
+- [ ] Rehearse the briefing to five minutes and make the central request explicit.
+- [ ] Run a final screen-reader-friendly structure check before using the materials at the department meeting.
